      "writtenOn": "2024-10-25T08:16:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is an interesting definition. If I configure a WANT_LGTM\u003dall, then that would mean that if I add a reviewer-by-email, that change is unsubmittable?\n\nIf so, then I could only recover by removing the reviewer which seems like an undesired behavior?",
      "revId": "99f7e90d507d79475bbe05479a2fde26f904fb07",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d29c28ca_3d99b4f3",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/submitrequirement/predicate/SubmitRequirementLabelExtensionPredicate.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-25T10:03:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intended workflow is like this:\n\n1. The change owner adds a user that doesn\u0027t have a Gerrit account as a reviewer on the change (reviewer by email).\n2. The reviewer gets an email about the review request\n3. The user opens the review link and Gerrit asks them to create an account.\n4. The user creates an account.\n5. The user approves the change\n\nAt 4. or latest at 5. the \"reviewer by email\" should be converted (automatically) into a \"real reviewer\", so that at this point the submit requirement gets fulfilled.\n\nHowever what happens at the moment is that the user is listed twice as a reviewer now, once by email and once by their Gerrit account. I consider this a bug, but fixing this is out of scope for this change. For now this workflow requires to remove the reviewer by email manually after 5. to make the change submittable. Depending on how many users are affected, we should just fix this bug.\n\nDoes this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "87f11132_bc7d81c9",
      "revId": "99f7e90d507d79475bbe05479a2fde26f904fb07",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
